================================================================================
EPSG geodetic parameter dataset
================================================================================

The `oxigeo-proj` crate embeds coordinate reference system (CRS) definitions
(coordinate systems, datums, ellipsoids, coordinate operations and their
parameters) derived from the EPSG Geodetic Parameter Dataset. The EPSG
Dataset is maintained by the International Association of Oil & Gas
Producers (IOGP) Geomatics Committee.

In accordance with the EPSG dataset's terms of use, the following
attribution is provided:

    Uses the EPSG Geodetic Parameter Dataset, ©International Association
    of Oil & Gas Producers (IOGP), reproduced/derived with permission
    under the terms of use published by IOGP at https://epsg.org/.

The values embedded in `oxigeo-proj` (CRS/datum/ellipsoid/operation
parameters, e.g. `crates/oxigeo-proj/src/epsg/`) are derived facts drawn
from the public EPSG registry (https://epsg.org/); no EPSG software or
copyrighted database files are redistributed, and the surrounding Rust
implementation is original work of this project licensed under
Apache-2.0. EPSG® and the EPSG dataset remain the property of IOGP.

================================================================================
Vendored third-party component: pathfinder_simd
================================================================================

`vendor/pathfinder_simd/` contains a vendored, lightly-patched copy of the
`pathfinder_simd` crate (version 0.5.6), originally published to
crates.io and developed as part of the Servo project's Pathfinder
rasterizer.

    Upstream project: pathfinder_simd (part of servo/pathfinder)
    Upstream repository: https://github.com/servo/pathfinder
    Upstream author: Patrick Walton <pcwalton@mimiga.net>
    Upstream license: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (dual-licensed; this project
                       elects to use it under the terms of the Apache
                       License, Version 2.0, consistent with the rest of
                       this repository)

This vendored copy is unmodified from upstream except for six intrinsic
renames in `src/arm/mod.rs` (`simd_minimum_number_nsz` ->
`simd_fmin`, `simd_maximum_number_nsz` -> `simd_fmax`) required to build
against current nightly Rust after upstream's `*_number_nsz` intrinsic
names were removed/renamed; see `vendor/pathfinder_simd/README.md` for
details. It is pulled in transitively (via `criterion`'s HTML report
feature and via `plotters`/`font-kit` from `oxigeo-jupyter`) and is
intended as an interim patch pending removal once those transitive paths
no longer require it.

